<!--
  Translation policy for Salah.

  Salah ships a **complete** Bangla translation (`app/src/main/res/values-bn/strings.xml`) and an
  English default (`app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml`). Every translatable string the English file
  defines has a Bangla value; the only strings that fall through to English are the three marked
  `translatable="false"` (`app_name` = "Salah", the Arabic `home_prayer_times_arabic` heading and the
  `—`/`…` placeholders), which carry no words to translate.

  The translation used to be deliberately **partial** — the explanatory wording that states what is an
  estimate, what Salah cannot verify, and which authority it does not claim to match stayed in English
  until it could be reviewed. Home, the Calendar, the Tools screen and every Settings screen (General,
  Appearance, Prayer times, Notifications and Adhan, Location, Calendar and About) are now translated in
  full, so that policy no longer applies and this file no longer suppresses `MissingTranslation`: adding
  a new string to the default file without a Bangla value is an error again. Completeness is
  additionally pinned by `LocalizationResourcesTest`, which reads the real resource files and asserts
  that the `tools_*` and `settings_*` families, the calculation options, the notification strings and
  the location strings all have a non-blank Bengali value written in Bengali script.

  Every other lint check keeps the severity configured in `app/build.gradle.kts`
  (`abortOnError = true`, `warningsAsErrors = false`).
-->
